Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:24:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S306p the known failures may only shrink, a gate
 (known-failures; the framework's thin path, T10; P-885; main's M63 and M65):
 queue/KNOWN_FAILURES.json lists every failing test and red gate on main with
 its register row and why, its first entries main's seven from its full suite
 on a fresh clone, each on P-810; scripts/queue/baseline.py checks its form
 and that it only shrinks along the history and against its last committed
 version, reads a run's lines to their test ids (FAILED and ERROR, ids up to
 the first ' - ' outside brackets), compares a run with it and drafts it; the
 shipped list's lock checks its form, rows and flakes, not its count; tests
 fail with each rule removed

